A quoted :INCLUDE inside a procedure body: both the target form
(include_quoted_target, error) and the placement (include_in_procedure,
warning) are wrong, and each should be reported once on its own range.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE LoadHelpers;
	:INCLUDE 'Common.StringHelpers';
	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE LoadHelpers;
	:INCLUDE 'Common.StringHelpers';
	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:2-2:10 warning include_in_procedure: ':INCLUDE' inside a procedure body is not supported
2:11-2:33 error include_quoted_target: ':INCLUDE' target must be an identifier, not a string: write ':INCLUDE Common.StringHelpers;'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:2-2:10 warning include_in_procedure: ':INCLUDE' inside a procedure body is not supported
2:11-2:33 error include_quoted_target: ':INCLUDE' target must be an identifier, not a string: write ':INCLUDE Common.StringHelpers;'
